document.querySelector('#method').innerHTML='<div class="card"><h2>Final findings and exact diagnostics</h2><p><a href="'+audit+'RESULTS.md">English results and interpretation</a> · <a href="'+audit+'analysis.json">Exact aggregate analysis</a></p>'+details('Concrete diagnostic cases, not teacher truth labels',d.manualDiagnostics)+details('Exported production subset-schema replay, including corrected attempts',d.schemaAudit)+'</div><div class="card"><h2>Controlled design</h2><p>PDF extraction (pdftotext), arithmetic/grid checks, local fingerprints and evidence-coordinate checks use local code and zero LLM tokens. Shared planning uses Sol medium. Original/repair generation uses the assigned generator. Fixed role/content/quality checks use Sol medium; the later cross-review quality layer deliberately uses all four configurations, distinguished by cross-prefixed cell IDs in the call ledger.</p><p>One source PDF is extracted into exact page-local text. Sol medium prepares a common 12-task plan. Those task instructions are AI-generated experimental controls, not professor-approved objectives or teacher labels. Every generator receives the same per-task prompt and the same growing common batch memory. After each task, the next memory representative is chosen by a prospectively fixed rotating arm, never by quality. The 12 cross-review candidates follow that same rotation. The shared trajectory is a single experimental draw, not independent repeated trials.</p><p>Production generator/role/content prompt builders, arithmetic checks and source/Bank/answer/demand assessment functions are reused. Native transport is an experimental nonstreaming OpenAI SDK client with retries disabled and a common 16,000-token completion envelope. The old 20-send/600k allowance is not used; the finite task design and existing single correction/repair loops bound work. This tests components against file-backed evidence; it does not execute production ingestion, live course retrieval, saving or publication.</p>'+details('Fixed task plan and explicit source coverage gaps',d.sharedPreparation)+details('Recorded limitations',d.limitations)+details('Execution controls',d.limits)+'<p><a href="'+audit+'results.json">Full current results</a> · <a href="'+audit+'authorization-evidence.json">Direct user authorization</a> · <a href="'+audit+'source/class15.pdf">Exact source PDF</a> · <a href="'+audit+'source/pages.json">Exact extracted pages</a> · <a href="'+audit+'code-pins.json">Code hashes</a></p></div>';
